  "slug": "cryo-structure-34d6",
  "summary": "Recent releases pair AlphaFold3 cofolding with curated covalent, ADC and ADMET resources for interaction and drug-property analysis.",
  "synthesis": "Most items share a theme of computational infrastructure for modelling molecular interactions, combining physics-based affinity calculation, curated interaction databases and predictive pipelines. BFEE3 provides a platform for absolute binding free energy calculations with an AI assistant and new DDM protocols. CovPDB 2.0 expands its covalent protein-ligand collection to about 6200 complexes and adds AlphaFold3 cofolding models with predicted cysteine ligandability. ADCdb 2.0 and DrugMAP 3.0 extend drug-level resources with ADMET endpoints and bioactivity data, the former covering 542 antibody-drug conjugates. Two preprints apply similar logic to specific problems: a transcriptomics and docking pipeline for human targets of plastic-derived chemicals, and an AI agent that designs selective protein interaction inhibitors. The new element is the combination of predicted co-folded structures with curated covalent and ADMET data in searchable resources. The items do not themselves report benchmark accuracy for these predictions.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
